error handling: raise exceptions instead of returning error tuples

Replace (result, error) tuples with exceptions for git operations and config loading.
Callers now catch GitError and ConfigError for cleaner error handling.

Changes:
- `create_worktree()` raises GitError on failure instead of returning None
- `open_pr()` raises GitError and returns URL directly
- `load_config()` raises ConfigError on invalid YAML or schema
- CLI commands catch specific exceptions and display user-friendly errors
- Moved `autocommit()` to git.py, added push and verbose parameters
- Added priority order for task file extensions: .lf > .md > other > bare name
- Comprehensive test coverage for new error handling paths
